asr-000065
00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:52.150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Allow me to say my opening remarks.

asr-000066
00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.870
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: To our distinguished chairperson, Kong Mika Swansing,

asr-000067
00:11:55.990 --> 00:12:00.150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: my fellow vice chairperson and colleagues in the House of Representatives,

asr-000068
00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.330
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to our tourism secretary, Dita Angara Mathay,

asr-000069
00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:07.010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the hardworking team of the Department of Tourism,

asr-000070
00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:15.310
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: good evening and welcome to the Department's budget briefing.

asr-000071
00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:21.430
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It is a privilege to preside over our deliberations on a sector that continues to generate jobs,

asr-000072
00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:25.250
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: sustain local enterprises, strengthen communities,

asr-000073
00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:28.770
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and showcase to the world why they should love the Philippines,

asr-000074
00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:34.930
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: while encouraging Filipinos and visitors alike to discover more to love across our country.

asr-000075
00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.530
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: This evening, we have the opportunity to hear from the Department of Tourism,

asr-000076
00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:41.730
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and to hear from our newly appointed Tourism Secretary, Sec. Dita Angara Mathay,

asr-000077
00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:46.150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: who has taken on the important responsibility of leading this vital sector.

asr-000078
00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:50.470
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: At the same time, it is our duty in Congress to constructively examine

asr-000079
00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:55.250
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: whether the Department's proposed budget responds to the needs of Philippine tourism,

asr-000080
00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:59.630
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and whether every peso we invest translates into more visitors,

asr-000081
00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:03.210
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: better infrastructure, stronger tourism enterprises,

asr-000082
00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:06.030
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and more opportunities for our people.

asr-000084
00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the importance of this sector is clear from the numbers.

asr-000085
00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:16.330
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: In 2025, tourism generated 2.27 trillion in tourism direct gross value added,

asr-000086
00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:23.390
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: equivalent to 8.1% of our GDP, while supporting millions of Filipino jobs.

asr-000087
00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:28.870
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism, therefore, is not merely about destinations and visitor arrivals.

asr-000088
00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:34.530
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It is a major contributor to our economy, and more importantly, to the livelihood of our people.

asr-000089
00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.490
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: These figures remind us why today's economy is so important,

asr-000090
00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.570
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and why this budget deliberation matters.

asr-000091
00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:43.850
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: We must ensure that the resources we provide to the Department

asr-000092
00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:49.610
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: are commensurate with both the opportunities and the challenges facing Philippine tourism.

asr-000093
00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:54.150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: As a tourism advocate, this is a sector I've always felt deeply connected.

asr-000094
00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:59.670
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Coming from Sorsogon, I have seen firsthand how tourism can transform communities

asr-000095
00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.030
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and create opportunities for our people.

asr-000096
00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:06.390
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Kasama po ako sa mga naniniwala that we should invest more in Philippine tourism.

asr-000097
00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:11.210
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And so I look forward to a productive and constructive deliberation,

asr-000098
00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.290
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: one where we recognize our gains, identify where we can do better,

asr-000099
00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.610
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and determine how Congress and the DOT can work together to make tourism

asr-000100
00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:23.970
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: an even stronger driver of inclusive and sustainable growth.

asr-000101
00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:28.570
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: With that, may I now invite Sec. Dita Angara-Mathai

asr-000102
00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.550
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to present the Department's proposed budget and priorities.

asr-000103
00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:34.010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Secretary, you may now proceed.

asr-000104
00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000105
00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.890
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Good evening, Madam Chairperson,

asr-000106
00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Honorable Members of the Committee,

asr-000107
00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.090
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and Distinguished Legislators.

asr-000108
00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:49.470
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism has been creating value for our economy and our people.

asr-000109
00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.490
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For Fiscal Year 2027,

asr-000110
00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:57.430
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: we intend to turn this momentum into greater economic value

asr-000111
00:14:57.430 --> 00:15:00.010
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and opportunities for more Filipinos.

asr-000112
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:06.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: May I now present the Department of Tourism's performance and direction for Fiscal Year

asr-000113
00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:07.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2027.

asr-000114
00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:24.430
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: First, our performance and accomplishments for 2025, second, the DOT's proposed budget

asr-000115
00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:31.710
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: under the Fiscal Year 2027 National Expenditure Program, and third, the additional funding

asr-000116
00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:41.030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: requirements needed to sustain our momentum and drive the next phase of tourism growth.

asr-000117
00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:48.310
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our mandate is to lead the planning, development, promotion and coordination of Philippine tourism.

asr-000118
00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:51.190
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We deliver this as one department.

asr-000119
00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:55.610
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The Central Office sets policy and strategic direction.

asr-000120
00:15:55.610 --> 00:16:01.730
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our regional offices develop destinations and tourism products, while our foreign offices

asr-000121
00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: build markets and generate international demand.

asr-000122
00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:15.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our agencies and corporations extend the Department's work across the tourism ecosystem, providing

asr-000123
00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:24.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: specialized support in infrastructure, heritage and destination development, dive tourism,

asr-000124
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:28.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: retirement, visitor services and tourism promotion.

asr-000125
00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:36.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In terms of funding, our NGAs are directly funded through appropriations in the GAA,

asr-000126
00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:42.880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: while our GOCCs generally operate under their corporate operating budgets.

asr-000127
00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:50.980
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For Fiscal Year 2027, both Duty Free Philippines and the Tourism Promotion Board have proposed

asr-000128
00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:57.940
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: budgetary support under the GAA.

asr-000129
00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:04.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our work is delivered through four core programs, with branding as a dedicated sub-program under

asr-000130
00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: market and product development.

asr-000131
00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Policy and Planning sets the direction for the development of tourism in Philippine

asr-000133
00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:15.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Industry Training develops our people.

asr-000134
00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:19.560
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Standards Development and Enforcement ensures quality.

asr-000135
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:24.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Market and Product Development turns our tourism assets into experiences that people

asr-000136
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:28.880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: can visit, enjoy and spend on.

asr-000137
00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Branding Campaign brings these experiences to the market, strengthening the Philippine

asr-000138
00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:38.460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: tourism brand and converting interest into actual travel.

asr-000140
00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:47.600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: These programs connect strategy, people, quality, products and markets into one tourism development

asr-000141
00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:53.010
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: system.

asr-000142
00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.770
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The programs must translate into measurable outcomes.

asr-000143
00:17:55.770 --> 00:18:03.310
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Direct Gross Value Added measures tourism's contribution to the economy.

asr-000144
00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:09.710
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism expenditures show how visitor activity translates into spending.

asr-000145
00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.370
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Employment tells us how that activity creates jobs.

asr-000148
00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:20.390
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: jobs. Tourism arrivals measure our ability to attract visitors to the Philippines. Together,

asr-000149
00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:27.990
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: these indicators tell us not only how tourism is performing, but how much value it has created

asr-000150
00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:36.320
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: for the country and for Filipinos. And the numbers show the scale of tourism's contribution to the

asr-000151
00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:46.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: economy. In 2025, tourism directly generated 2.27 trillion in economic value, equivalent to 8.1%

asr-000152
00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:55.600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: of our GDP. Tourism spending was also substantial, with 3.26 trillion pesos generated by domestic

asr-000153
00:18:55.600 --> 00:19:04.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: tourism and 698 billion pesos from international visitors. This shows that tourism is a major

asr-000154
00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: economic sector that drives tourism.

asr-000155
00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:11.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism spending generates jobs and supports businesses and livelihoods across the country.

asr-000156
00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:20.830
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Let's look closely into the economic value of tourism, particularly to the creation of job

asr-000157
00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:29.530
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: opportunities and livelihoods for millions of Filipinos. In 2025, tourism supported 7.7 million

asr-000158
00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:37.590
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: jobs, representing 15.7% of total employment in the country. That is nearly

asr-000160
00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:44.930
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: One in every six working Filipinos with tourism employment continuing to grow from 5.4 million in

asr-000161
00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:55.180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2021. That economic activity is supported by continued tourism demand. From January to July

asr-000162
00:19:55.180 --> 00:20:06.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2026, international visitor arrivals reached 3.93 million, up by 1.5% from 3.87 million

asr-000163
00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:10.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: during the same period last year. The United States,

asr-000164
00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:18.080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: of course, remains our largest source market, followed by South Korea and Japan, while China

asr-000165
00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:24.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: has returned to make top-five markets. The challenge now is to build on these key markets

asr-000166
00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:32.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and accelerate international tourist arrivals through the rest of the year.

asr-000167
00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:39.280
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The current performance builds on the recovery achieved over the past three years. Visitor

asr-000168
00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:45.200
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: arrivals increased from 5.48 million in 2023

asr-000169
00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: to 6.48 million in 2025,

asr-000171
00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: representing overall growth of 18.4 percent.

asr-000172
00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:57.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Sustaining that upward trajectory now requires us to compete more effectively for a larger

asr-000173
00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: share of the regional tourism market.

asr-000174
00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:07.840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: But our performance must also be viewed with an increasingly competitive ASEAN tourism

asr-000175
00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:08.280
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: market.

asr-000176
00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:16.080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In 2025, the Philippines ranked 6th in ASEAN, improving from 7th place in 2024.

asr-000177
00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:24.800
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yet, with 6.48 million arrivals, we captured only 5 percent of the regional market shown

asr-000178
00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:25.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: here.

asr-000179
00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:31.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our improved ranking is encouraging, but the opportunity is much larger.

asr-000180
00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:37.080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our task ahead is to compete for a greater share of ASEAN tourist arrivals.

asr-000181
00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Growing Tourism Market

asr-000182
00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:48.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Beyond tourist volume, our objective is to increase the economic value generated by every

asr-000183
00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:48.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: visit.

asr-000184
00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:57.480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The Philippines remained 5th in ASEAN in tourism receipts in 2025, generating about 12.15

asr-000185
00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:58.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: billion U.S. dollars.

asr-000186
00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:06.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: While receipts declined slightly from 2024, our regional position was maintained despite

asr-000187
00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: higher travel costs.

asr-000188
00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:12.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and spending in selected categories.

asr-000189
00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:19.100
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The opportunity now is to attract more visitors and generate greater value from every visit.

asr-000190
00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:27.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our regional position must also be viewed in the context of the resources behind tourism

asr-000191
00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:28.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: development.

asr-000192
00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:36.700
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In 2025, the Philippines operated with about 49.7 million dollars, significantly below

asr-000193
00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:40.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: the tourism budget of the major ASEAN destinations shown here.

asr-000194
00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:50.500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yet, tourism already contributes 2.27 trillion to our economy and supports 7.7 million Philippine

asr-000195
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:51.500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: jobs.

asr-000196
00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:57.960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We are emphasizing that greater strategic investment in tourism can unlock a much larger

asr-000197
00:22:57.960 --> 00:23:04.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: opportunity as it can bring more tourists, generate more spending, create more jobs,

asr-000198
00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:11.490
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and spread socio-economic growth across our regions.

asr-000199
00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:12.490
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The investment opportunity becomes even more important.

asr-000200
00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:17.210
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The opportunity becomes even clearer when we look at tourism marketing budgets of ASEAN

asr-000201
00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:19.070
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: member states.

asr-000202
00:23:19.070 --> 00:23:28.190
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In 2025, the Philippines invested 86.68 million dollars below several ASEAN competitors while

asr-000203
00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:37.090
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: generating 74,758 tourist arrivals for every 1 million dollars in government marketing

asr-000204
00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:38.090
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: investment.

asr-000205
00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:44.090
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: One might say that Vietnam's smaller government branding budget is relatively lower than the Philippines,

asr-000206
00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:55.490
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: but it may be well to note that the Vietnam's budget is largely complemented by strong private sector investment in tourism development, particularly the Sun Group.

asr-000207
00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:04.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The gains we have achieved so far provide a strong foundation for pursuing that opportunity.

asr-000208
00:24:04.760 --> 00:24:14.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Behind these numbers are concrete interventions that strengthen our people, destinations, tourism products, and access to markets.

asr-000209
00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:21.980
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Let me now highlight some of the department's key accomplishments for 2025 and 2026.

asr-000210
00:24:24.220 --> 00:24:29.540
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We begin with the people who deliver the tourism experience.

asr-000211
00:24:29.540 --> 00:24:35.540
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: As of July 2026, the department has trained 52,960.

asr-000212
00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:43.640
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The department has trained 168 participants nationwide, with more than half coming directly from the tourism and hospitality industry.

asr-000213
00:24:44.640 --> 00:24:52.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We might have a slight reduction in number of trained participants this year due to recalibration and change in targeted participants,

asr-000214
00:24:52.900 --> 00:25:00.260
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: but it is noteworthy that by strengthening the capabilities of our workforce, academe, and LGUs,

asr-000215
00:25:00.520 --> 00:25:05.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: we build the service quality and local capacity needed for a more competitive tourism.

asr-000216
00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:21.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Apart from training, we also highlight the importance of accreditation of tourism enterprises and frontliners as it protects the quality of the tourism experience.

asr-000217
00:25:21.380 --> 00:25:38.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: DOT-accredited tourism enterprises and frontliners increased by 35% from 11,545 in 2023 to 15,592 as of June 2026.

asr-000218
00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:49.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: This year, may I note that we are going beyond accreditation numbers by strengthening compliance, monitoring, renewal, and service standards.

asr-000219
00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:57.800
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: All these ensure that accreditation becomes a stronger mark of quality and confidence in Philippine tourism.

asr-000220
00:26:01.300 --> 00:26:05.560
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Quality tourism products must also be connected to the markets that sustain them.

asr-000221
00:26:06.280 --> 00:26:11.420
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: As of September 2026, 20 new international routes have been created.

asr-000222
00:26:11.640 --> 00:26:16.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: These routes have been launched, opening more gateways to destinations across the country.

asr-000223
00:26:17.200 --> 00:26:26.260
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Another 13 routes are set to launch, bringing projected additional capacity to more than 472,000 seats by year-end.

asr-000224
00:26:28.840 --> 00:26:34.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Beyond expanding access, we are positioning the Philippines in high-value tourism markets.

asr-000225
00:26:35.220 --> 00:26:40.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: After the Philippines was recognized as the world's number one retirement destination,

asr-000226
00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:43.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: the Philippine Retirement Authority,

asr-000227
00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:50.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: saw average SRRV applications jump from 15 to 25 per day,

asr-000228
00:26:50.660 --> 00:26:54.480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: a 67% increase following the recognition.

asr-000229
00:26:55.640 --> 00:26:57.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The opportunity is significant.

asr-000230
00:26:58.180 --> 00:27:04.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In July 2026, Bank of Singapore reported that the global longevity economy,

asr-000231
00:27:05.440 --> 00:27:08.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: driven by the growing spending power of older and retired consumers,

asr-000232
00:27:09.680 --> 00:27:13.460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: is valued at $3 trillion and projected to reach,

asr-000233
00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:15.880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: $5.4 trillion in 2034.

asr-000234
00:27:15.880 --> 00:27:23.020
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Travel and leisure are identified among the sectors positioned to benefit from this growth.

asr-000235
00:27:24.060 --> 00:27:26.620
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: As the world's top-ranked retirement destination,

asr-000236
00:27:26.620 --> 00:27:32.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: the Philippines is well-positioned to capture a greater share of this growing global market.

asr-000237
00:27:33.020 --> 00:27:39.780
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We are also building on our global leadership in dive tourism,

asr-000238
00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:43.780
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: one of the Philippines' strongest high-value tourism products.

asr-000240
00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:53.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: is estimated to generate $1.3 billion in tourism revenue, supported by our world-class marine

asr-000241
00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:58.800
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: biodiversity, in seven consecutive years as the world's leading dive destination.

asr-000242
00:27:59.540 --> 00:28:06.200
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: But the opportunity is larger. The Philippine Commission on Sports, School with Diving,

asr-000243
00:28:06.200 --> 00:28:15.180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: has identified 29 dive destination clusters and 956 dive sites nationwide.

asr-000244
00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:20.620
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Many of which are still emerging or undergoing development and validation.

asr-000245
00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:28.020
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Even under a conservative growth scenario, annual dive tourism revenue is projected to reach

asr-000246
00:28:28.020 --> 00:28:33.780
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: $100.5 billion by 2030, from $73 billion in 2023.

asr-000247
00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:43.960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: BCSSD has certified 330 dive professionals and individuals as of June 2026.

asr-000249
00:28:45.260 --> 00:28:52.100
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: This builds on the strong expansion in certifications since 2023 and reflects the continued development

asr-000250
00:28:52.100 --> 00:28:58.680
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: of the skilled workforce needed to support a safe, professional, and competitive Philippine dive industry.

asr-000251
00:28:59.600 --> 00:29:05.840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We are also expanding cruise tourism as a gateway to multiple Philippine destinations

asr-000252
00:29:05.840 --> 00:29:14.420
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: within a single journey. Cruise calls recovered to 136 in 2025 and are projected to reach

asr-000253
00:29:14.420 --> 00:29:24.100
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 155 calls across 38 destinations by 2027, with bookings already extending into 2028.

asr-000254
00:29:24.800 --> 00:29:30.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The opportunity is to convert each port call into greater local economic activity,

asr-000255
00:29:30.660 --> 00:29:35.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: to shore excursions, longer stays, and onward travel.

asr-000256
00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:43.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Growth is already extending beyond traditional gateways, with cruise calls in the Visayas projected to double,

asr-000257
00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:52.760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: from 14 in 2026 to 28 in 2027, while new destinations are being assessed for future itineraries.

asr-000258
00:29:54.520 --> 00:29:59.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Supporting this growth is the Cruise Visa Waiver Program, which makes it easier

asr-000263
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:03.440
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: for cruise passengers to enter and experience the Philippines.

asr-000264
00:30:04.440 --> 00:30:13.480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Since its launch in 2024, 16,563 waivers have been issued as of June 2026,

asr-000265
00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:17.980
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: with 99.8% issued to Chinese nationals.

asr-000266
00:30:18.760 --> 00:30:24.880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Notably, the 7,066 waivers issued in the first half of 2026

asr-000267
00:30:24.880 --> 00:30:29.180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: already exceeded the full year total for 2025.

asr-000268
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:35.600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The strong uptake demonstrates the importance of streamlined travel facilitation

asr-000269
00:30:35.600 --> 00:30:39.120
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: in unlocking not just the Chinese cruise market,

asr-000270
00:30:39.520 --> 00:30:45.460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: but all our key and emerging markets by supporting further cruise tourism growth.

asr-000271
00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:50.580
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We are seeing the same conversion from global recognition

asr-000272
00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:53.680
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: to economic activity in gastronomy tourism.

asr-000273
00:30:54.620 --> 00:30:59.640
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The inaugural Michelin Guide Philippines recognized 108 establishments,

asr-000274
00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:01.400
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: placing our culinary seasonings,

asr-000275
00:31:01.440 --> 00:31:06.260
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: following the Michelin Guide announcement,

asr-000276
00:31:06.820 --> 00:31:14.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: DOT partner payment network data showed transactions increased by 33.6%,

asr-000277
00:31:14.380 --> 00:31:20.860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: while transaction value grew by 22.6% in the fourth quarter of 2025,

asr-000278
00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:23.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: compared with the same period of 2024.

asr-000279
00:31:24.840 --> 00:31:28.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Filipino cuisine is becoming more than a tourism experience.

asr-000280
00:31:28.380 --> 00:31:31.420
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: It is becoming a reason to travel to the Philippines.

asr-000281
00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:42.240
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The global recognition is helping us bring travelers beyond our already established destinations,

asr-000282
00:31:42.800 --> 00:31:43.800
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: such as Boracay.

asr-000283
00:31:44.680 --> 00:31:48.140
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Emerging destinations are gaining international attention

asr-000284
00:31:48.140 --> 00:31:50.120
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and recording significant growth.

asr-000285
00:31:51.060 --> 00:31:57.840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourist arrivals increased by 302% in Batanes and 110% in Camiguin,

asr-000286
00:31:57.840 --> 00:32:01.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: while Cavite and El Nido also posted strong gains,

asr-000287
00:32:02.320 --> 00:32:03.120
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: following greater,

asr-000288
00:32:03.260 --> 00:32:10.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: international visibility. Each recognized destination becomes a gateway to nearby places,

asr-000289
00:32:10.840 --> 00:32:16.480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: inviting travelers to explore farther and discover a thousand more reasons to love

asr-000290
00:32:16.480 --> 00:32:26.940
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: the Philippines. The Philippines' rise among non-OIC destinations in the 2026 Global Muslim

asr-000291
00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:34.180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Travel Index demonstrates the results of our sustained investment in halal and Muslim-friendly

asr-000292
00:32:34.180 --> 00:32:41.500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: tourism. With 70 Muslim-friendly accommodation establishments nationwide, we are strengthening

asr-000293
00:32:41.500 --> 00:32:47.640
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: destination readiness to diversify our source markets and capture a greater share of the

asr-000294
00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:54.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: growing global Muslim travel market. We have strengthened our people, our standards, and

asr-000295
00:32:54.660 --> 00:33:00.540
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: experiences and destinations that make the Philippines worth discovering. The next step

asr-000296
00:33:00.540 --> 00:33:02.580
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: is to bring these stories to the market.

asr-000297
00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:04.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Through Discover,

asr-000298
00:33:04.180 --> 00:33:10.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: More to Love, we bring together airlines, hotels, and tourism partners to encourage

asr-000299
00:33:10.340 --> 00:33:16.660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Filipinos to explore more of the country. Here is a short video that provides a glimpse

asr-000300
